WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.402
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.290
SPEAKER: At Google
data centers, we

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.990
have a relentless
focus on performance.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.210
Our data centers are
more than just buildings

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.760
with a collection of
machines wired together.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.010
They host clusters of
hundreds of thousands

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.680
of servers in locations
across the globe

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.450
that need to act as
a unified network.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.930
So what does it take to
operate and build them

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.390
efficiently at massive scale?

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.270
It all comes down to
four core principles--

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:37.190
performance, availability,
security, and sustainability.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.830
To optimize for
performance, we don't rely

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.570
on off-the-shelf components.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.310
We customize the
design and build

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.230
of almost every
part of the stack

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.940
for ultra high performance.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.710
This includes electrical
substations, servers, racks,

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.620
and even how we
operate cooling plants.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.040
You might think that means
we're using high-end computers.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.010
But at Google, we build
from the bottom up.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.800
Commodity hardware
underpins our custom tech

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.750
stack that runs
hundreds of thousands

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.570
of jobs across these machines
to give you distributed

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.220
performance and scale.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.220
But this doesn't mean we're
using the desktop computer

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.630
you're used to at home.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.700
Although your computer
has a lot of technology

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.890
that's optimized
for how you use it,

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.890
our data center servers use
only the components needed

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.960
for lean, high performance.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.680
When multiplied
by the thousands,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.230
we provide you a sweet spot
between performance and cost.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:33.440
Google Cloud servers are built
using the Google Titan chip

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.540
from the time of manufacturing.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:39.110
Titan helps secure every server
through its entire lifecycle.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.510
It uses Root of Trust
technology, which

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.600
cryptographically ensures that
the chip hasn't been tampered

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.740
with and significantly reduces
the chance of vulnerabilities.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:51.530
But what happens if
the machine fails?

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.750
Billions of users
depend on our services

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.660
being up and running
24/7, so Google

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.490
uses a fault-tolerant
design that's

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:01.580
maintainable from
concept to operations.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.380
At the infrastructure
level, this

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.410
boils down to constant
monitoring of every hardware

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.710
component, electrical,
and mechanical system

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:15.080
for configuration, activity,
environmental, and error data.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.360
We use machine learning
and machine failure

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.690
diagnostic tools to
suggest corrective actions.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.960
And because we're constantly
upgrading and reconfiguring

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.110
our infrastructure, our
hardware operations teams

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.440
do deployments, maintenance,
upgrades, and repairs

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.110
of all hardware 24/7.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.510
This all comes with
the key responsibility

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.440
of protecting and securing our
data centers for every user

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.300
and Google Cloud customer.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.150
More on that next time on
"Discovering Data Centers."

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

